hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"308","Narrated by Muhammad bin Yahya, narrated by Ruh bin Ubadah, on the authority of Handala, who said: I heard Ikrimah bin Khalid bin Al-Aas, speaking to Tawus, that A man said to Abdullah bin Omar: Will you not fight? Abdullah bin Omar said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Islam is built on five things: the testimony that there is no god but God, And establishing prayer, paying zakat, fasting Ramadan, and performing Hajj to the House.”"
"309","Narrated by Ahmad bin Mansour Al-Ramadi, by Abu Al-Nadr, by Asim, who is the son of Muhammad bin Zaid bin Abdullah bin Omar bin Al-Khattab, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Islam is built on five things: the testimony that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is the Messenger God, and establishing prayer, paying zakat, performing Hajj to the House, and fasting Ramadan.” Muhammad bin Yahya narrated it, Ahmad bin Yunus narrated it, Asim narrated it, Waqid bin Muhammad bin Zaid told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: In the same way. Abu Bakr said: I mentioned the paths of this hadith in the Book of Faith."
